
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <meta name="description" content="HTML Skeleton Workflow - A guide to creating a well-structured HTML5 document.">
    <meta name="author" content="Caraga State University - College of Information and Computing Sciences">

    <title>The HTML Skeleton</title>
</head>

<body>

    <!-- HEADER -->
    <header>
        <p>CARAGA STATE UNIVERSITY - COLLEGE OF INFORMATION AND COMPUTING SCIENCES</p>
        <p>2026</p>

        <h1>The &lt;HTML&gt; Skeleton</h1>

        <p>
            <strong>Goal:</strong>
            Turn your sketch and your Phase 1 content into a
            well-structured HTML page with no styling.
        </p>

        <p>
            Lecturer: Princess Beverly R. Ala-an
        </p>
    </header>


    <!-- MAIN CONTENT -->
    <main>

        <!-- INTRODUCTION -->
        <section id="introduction">

            <h2>HTML Skeleton Workflow</h2>

            <p>
                Learn how to create a properly structured HTML5 document
                by following these eight stages.
            </p>

        </section>


        <!-- FIRST WORKFLOW SECTION -->
        <section id="workflow-stage-one">

            <h2>Stages 01-04</h2>

            <!-- STAGE 01 -->
            <article id="stage-01">

                <h3>Stage 01 - CREATION</h3>

                <p>
                    Create a project folder with an index.html file
                    and an images folder.
                </p>

                <ul>
                    <li>Create a project folder.</li>
                    <li>Create an index.html file.</li>
                    <li>Create an images folder.</li>
                </ul>

            </article>


            <!-- STAGE 02 -->
            <article id="stage-02">

                <h3>Stage 02 - HTML5 DOC</h3>

                <p>
                    Start from a valid HTML5 document containing
                    the required document structure.
                </p>

                <ul>
                    <li>DOCTYPE declaration</li>
                    <li>HTML element with a lang attribute</li>
                    <li>Head element</li>
                    <li>Meta charset</li>
                    <li>Meta viewport</li>
                    <li>Descriptive title</li>
                </ul>

            </article>


            <!-- STAGE 03 -->
            <article id="stage-03">

                <h3>Stage 03 - STRUCTURE</h3>

                <p>
                    Build a page structure from your sketch using
                    appropriate semantic HTML elements.
                </p>

                <ul>
                    <li>Header</li>
                    <li>Navigation</li>
                    <li>Main content</li>
                    <li>Section</li>
                    <li>Article</li>
                    <li>Aside</li>
                    <li>Footer</li>
                </ul>

            </article>


            <!-- STAGE 04 -->
            <article id="stage-04">

                <h3>Stage 04 - CONTENT</h3>

                <p>
                    Add all your Phase 1 content using the correct
                    HTML elements.
                </p>

                <ul>
                    <li>Headings for sections</li>
                    <li>Paragraphs</li>
                    <li>Lists</li>
                    <li>Links</li>
                    <li>Images with meaningful alt text</li>
                    <li>Figures with figcaptions</li>
                </ul>

                <figure>
                    <img
                        src="images/html-skeleton.png"
                        alt="Illustration showing the basic structure of an HTML5 document"
                    >
                    <figcaption>
                        Figure 1. Basic HTML5 document structure.
                    </figcaption>
                </figure>

            </article>

        </section>


        <!-- SECOND WORKFLOW SECTION -->
        <section id="workflow-stage-two">

            <h2>Stages 05-08</h2>

            <!-- STAGE 05 -->
            <article id="stage-05">

                <h3>Stage 05 - BUILD NAV</h3>

                <p>
                    Build navigation with links that work.
                    Use anchors to connect sections or links to other pages.
                </p>

                <ul>
                    <li>Use anchor elements.</li>
                    <li>Link to the correct sections or pages.</li>
                    <li>Make sure every link has a meaningful destination.</li>
                </ul>

                <nav aria-label="Workflow navigation">
                    <ul>
                        <li><a href="#stage-01">Stage 01 - Creation</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#stage-02">Stage 02 - HTML5 Document</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#stage-03">Stage 03 - Structure</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#stage-04">Stage 04 - Content</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#stage-05">Stage 05 - Build Nav</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#stage-06">Stage 06 - Don'ts</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#stage-07">Stage 07 - Run It</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#stage-08">Stage 08 - Submission</a></li>
                    </ul>
                </nav>

            </article>


            <!-- STAGE 06 -->
            <article id="stage-06">

                <h3>Stage 06 - DON'TS</h3>

                <p>
                    Do not use CSS, style attributes, or outdated HTML tags.
                    The page will look plain, and that is expected.
                </p>

                <ul>
                    <li>Do not use CSS.</li>
                    <li>Do not use inline styles.</li>
                    <li>Do not use outdated HTML tags.</li>
                    <li>Focus on proper HTML structure.</li>
                </ul>

            </article>


            <!-- STAGE 07 -->
            <article id="stage-07">

                <h3>Stage 07 - RUN IT</h3>

                <p>
                    Run your page in a web browser and fix every error
                    you can find.
                </p>

                <ol>
                    <li>Open your project in Visual Studio Code.</li>
                    <li>Open your index.html file.</li>
                    <li>Run the page using a web browser.</li>
                    <li>Check your links and content.</li>
                    <li>Fix any errors you find.</li>
                </ol>

            </article>


            <!-- STAGE 08 -->
            <article id="stage-08">

                <h3>Stage 08 - SUBMISSION</h3>

                <p>
                    Commit all of your work to GitHub.
                    Make sure screenshots of the running page are
                    included in your repository.
                </p>

                <ul>
                    <li>Commit your HTML project.</li>
                    <li>Push your files to GitHub.</li>
                    <li>Include screenshots of your running page.</li>
                    <li>Attach your repository link for submission.</li>
                </ul>

                <p>
                    Visit
                    <a href="https://github.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                        GitHub
                    </a>
                    to access your repository.
                </p>

            </article>

        </section>


        <!-- ADDITIONAL INFORMATION -->
        <aside>

            <h2>Important Reminder</h2>

            <p>
                Always use proper HTML5 semantic elements.
                Remember that this activity focuses on the structure
                and organization of an HTML document, not its appearance.
            </p>

        </aside>

    </main>


    <!-- FOOTER -->
    <footer>

        <p>
